# The PDF object model (PDF 1.7 spec §7.3): the eight basic object types, an indirect object's `N G obj ...
# endobj` wrapper, and the cross-reference table plus trailer that a whole file needs to be readable at all.
# Separate from ../code.tree's content-stream operator catalog on purpose — a content stream is bytes INSIDE one
# of these objects (a stream object's data), not a variant of one. `pdf-string` covers both PDF string syntaxes
# (parenthesized literal and hex `<...>`) uniformly as decoded text; nothing downstream needs to know which
# syntax produced it, the same way JSON's own escape-decoding collapses to one `like text` regardless of how a
# character was written in the source.

form pdf-value
  case pdf-null
  case pdf-boolean
    link value, like boolean
  case pdf-number
    link value, like decimal
  case pdf-string
    link value, like text
  case pdf-name
    link value, like text
  case pdf-array
    link items
      like list
        like pdf-value
  case pdf-dictionary
    link entries
      like list
        like pdf-entry
  case pdf-reference
    link object-number, like number
    link generation, like number

form pdf-entry
  link key, like text
  link value, like pdf-value

form pdf-indirect-object
  link object-number, like number
  link generation, like number
  link value, like pdf-value

# `in-use`: PDF's own term is "free" vs "in use" (the xref table's `f`/`n` marker) rather than a positive
# boolean, but `in-use` is what CLAUDE.md's naming rule wants (a controlled-vocabulary flag reads as what IS
# true, not its negation).
form pdf-xref-entry
  link offset, like number
  link generation, like number
  link in-use, like boolean

form pdf-xref-table
  link start, like number
  link entries
    like list
      like pdf-xref-entry

# `root` is `like pdf-value`, not a narrower reference-only type: `pdf-reference` is a CASE of `pdf-value`'s
# tagged union, not a form of its own, so nothing else could be named here — real PDF has the same looseness,
# a trailer's `/Root` is conventionally a reference but nothing in the object model itself enforces that.
form pdf-trailer
  link size, like number
  link root, like pdf-value
